## Goal
Add first-class PostgreSQL partition metadata and guarded partition management so partitioned schemas are not represented as ordinary tables with missing semantics.

## Scope
- introspect partitioned tables and partition children;
- partition key columns/expressions and strategy: RANGE / LIST / HASH;
- parent/child relationship in Explorer and table workbench;
- create partitioned table where supported by A09 table creation flow;
- attach/detach partition;
- create partition with bounds;
- view/generate DDL;
- dependency/risk preview before detach/drop;
- SQLite capability-gated.

## Safety
- attaching/detaching can be expensive or lock-heavy: classify as mutation/long-running where appropriate;
- never fabricate bounds or infer a safe partition operation from naming conventions;
- destructive drop remains confirmation-gated.

## Acceptance
- partition hierarchy renders deterministically for live PG fixture;
- RANGE/LIST/HASH metadata round-trips correctly;
- attach/detach/create-partition uses canonical A01 mutation pipeline;
- unsupported operations are disabled with explicit reason;
- Explorer refresh updates only affected schema/table subtree;
- provider/service/native UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(schema): add PostgreSQL partition management`

