## Goal
Add a safe PostgreSQL Extensions workbench for discovering installed/available extensions and managing extension lifecycle through canonical application actions.

## Scope
- list installed extensions, version, schema, description;
- list available extensions/versions where provider permits;
- create extension;
- update extension version;
- drop extension;
- extension-owned object/dependency warning;
- DDL preview;
- Explorer node under database/schema administration area;
- SQLite capability-gated.

## Safety
- extension CREATE/UPDATE/DROP classified Administrative/Destructive as appropriate;
- superuser/permission failure surfaced structurally;
- no automatic extension install/update;
- dependency/cascade effects visible before drop.

## Acceptance
- installed extension metadata is correct on live PostgreSQL;
- create/update/drop routes through application/service layer;
- unsupported or privilege-restricted actions are disabled/explained;
- no direct `pg_extension` mutation logic in UI;
- provider/service/native UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(schema): add PostgreSQL extensions workbench`

