## Goal
Add first-class PostgreSQL Row-Level Security policy inspection and management as part of the Security workbench.

## Scope
- inspect RLS enabled/forced state per table;
- list policies with command scope, roles, USING and WITH CHECK expressions;
- enable/disable RLS;
- force/unforce RLS;
- create/alter/drop policy;
- preview exact SQL;
- show referenced roles and target table;
- SQLite capability-gated.

## Safety
- policy changes can immediately change application data visibility/write behavior;
- classify policy mutation as Administrative/Mutation and require explicit confirmation;
- never auto-simplify or rewrite policy expressions;
- preserve SQL expressions losslessly.

## Acceptance
- live PG fixture proves SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE policy metadata;
- enable/force state round-trips correctly;
- create/alter/drop uses canonical mutation pipeline;
- policy body/source is preserved exactly enough for safe edit/review;
- role references resolve to Security workbench;
- provider/service/native UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(security): add PostgreSQL row-level security policies`

