## Goal
Add a dedicated transaction/session-state surface so users can understand long-lived transactions, idle-in-transaction risk, backend state and current session context.

## Scope
PostgreSQL:
- transaction age;
- backend/session age;
- idle in transaction;
- transaction start/query start;
- wait state;
- backend xact identifiers where meaningful;
- current database/user/application/client;
- session settings summary where safe;
- open current query in editor;
- cancel/terminate through D01 canonical actions.

SQLite:
- expose only meaningful local transaction state available through current connection/runtime; do not fake server sessions.

## Acceptance
- idle-in-transaction sessions are distinguishable from active queries;
- transaction ages are calculated/displayed consistently;
- exact backend identity is preserved across actions;
- refresh stops when inactive;
- no direct monitoring SQL in renderer;
- live PG provider/service/native UI tests.

Merge independently after D01.
Suggested commit: `feat(monitoring): add transaction and session state inspector`

